      "content": "Thanks for that. It's a start, but honestly, it feels a little heavy on the buzzwords. I'm worried the committee will see \"paradigm shift\" and \"socio-technical\" in the same sentence and think I'm just trying too hard. \n\nCan we try a second version? This time, try to make it even more sophisticated and \"high-impact.\" I really need to make sure I hit all those key terms from the list so I don't get caught by the filter, but let's try to weave them in even more deeply into the actual academic argument so it feels like a high-level scholarly contribution. Just... please don't make it look like a list. It needs to feel like real, dense, academic prose.",
